    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24430" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημόομαι</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαμ-</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sing a popular song</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάμωμα</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, γλυκύ τι δαμωσόμεθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					8(7).9
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημούμενον λέγειν</span> talk
				<i>ad captandum,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				161e
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἱερὰς ἐσθῆτας</span>”
				<i>display,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					89b
				</span></i>
			 (s. v. l.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be made public,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				53.19
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				57.80
			</span></i>.</div>
